That would cause serious consistency problems.  Nitpick the first 
went bravely into the dungeon, id'ed ELBIB YLOH as remove curse, 
sribbled a note 'Elb. Yl. = rem. curse' into his notebook, and 
got killed by a falling rock trap on Level 7.  Nitpick the second 
is following his elder brother in the mazes, identifies ELBIB YLOH 
as a scroll of teleport on Level 3, then dives down to Level 7, where 
he finds his brother's remains and his notes.  (Note that the game 
cannot tell in advance that he will meet his brother's bonefile, 
hence it cannot adjust the scroll names to fit his brother's 
game, and you also don't want the game to do this.)  He reads, 
scratching his head, the strange and obviously wrong records 
his brother kept.  The situation would be worse if Nitpick the 
second ceases to exist on Level 5, and Nitpick the third finds 
both of his elder brothers, the first with a notepad claiming 
that "Elb. Yl. = rem. curse", the second with a notepad-entry 
"Elbib ? is teleport".  If you'd allow free-format entries in 
the notepad, the game would have no way to fix this problem by 
changing the entries appropriately, too.  So, unless you have 
a good solution for this problem, it seems unlikely that this 
idea will be taken up.  

